## Bug-Introducing Commits
BIC: d12f7fdbe42329c2e1e3faea654c884426255202

## Reasoning

**(1) Investigation:** I ran `git log -p --follow` on `LocalInspectionsPass.java` to trace the history of the exact line touched by the fix commit (the `tooltip = XmlStringUtil.wrapInHtml(...)` assignment). This surfaced every prior version of that line, allowing me to locate the commit where the buggy form (`wrapInHtml(...) + link ;` instead of `wrapInHtml((...) + link);`) was first introduced.

**(2) The introducing change:** Commit `d12f7fdbe42329c2e1e3faea654c884426255202` (Alexey Kudravtsev, 2015-05-26) refactored an if/else block:
```java
if (message.startsWith("<html>")) {
  tooltip = XmlStringUtil.wrapInHtml(XmlStringUtil.stripHtml(message) + link);
}
else {
  tooltip = XmlStringUtil.wrapInHtml(XmlStringUtil.escapeString(message) + link);
}
```
into a single ternary expression:
```java
tooltip = XmlStringUtil.wrapInHtml(message.startsWith("<html>") ? XmlStringUtil.stripHtml(message): XmlStringUtil.escapeString(message)) + link ;
```
In doing so, the closing parenthesis of `wrapInHtml(...)` was misplaced — `link` ended up concatenated *outside* the `wrapInHtml()` call instead of inside it as in both original branches. This changes the resulting HTML tooltip structure (the `link` fragment is no longer part of the wrapped HTML body), which is exactly the defect that commit `8f5cb78051a109986916d97481c994275622de7b` fixes by moving `link` back inside the parentheses.

**(3) Evidence:** The fix commit's diff is a pure inverse of this refactor's mistake — it only relocates the closing parenthesis to include `+ link` inside `wrapInHtml(...)`, restoring the original (pre-refactor) semantics where `link` was always wrapped inside the HTML together with the message. No other commit touches this line between `d12f7fdbe42329c2e1e3faea654c884426255202` and the fix, confirming this is the sole origin of the bug.

I'm highly confident in this identification since the diff evidence is direct and unambiguous (an exact structural inverse of the fix), and no commit messages were needed to reach this conclusion.

